---
// A before-and-after pair for one preflight message: a terse technical line,
// and the same finding said to the customer in plain language. The words are
// invented for this page. Neither line is real system output, and this is not a
// screen. Labelled as an illustrative example.
//
// Real HTML, so axe can check the contrast. "Before" is a dashed box in the
// monospace face, "after" a solid accent box in the body face, so the
// difference does not depend on colour alone. Side by side from 40rem, stacked
// below that.
---

<figure class="pm">
  <p class="illus-tag">Illustrative example: not real system output</p>
  <div class="pm__grid">
    <div class="pm__panel pm__panel--before" role="group" aria-labelledby="pm-before">
      <p class="pm__head" id="pm-before">Before: technical</p>
      <p class="pm__line pm__line--tech">Bleed: 0 mm. Required: 3 mm.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pm__panel pm__panel--after" role="group" aria-labelledby="pm-after">
      <p class="pm__head" id="pm-after">After: friendly</p>
      <p class="pm__kind">Fixed for you</p>
      <p class="pm__line">
        Your design runs right to the edge, so we’ve added a little extra around it (bleed) so nothing gets trimmed off.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="illus-caption">
    The same finding, said two ways. The customer reads the second one.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
